# Copy this to .env and fill in real values. Nothing here is a secret by
# itself — this file is just documentation of what the app expects.

# Local Postgres (installed via `brew install postgresql@16`, running as a
# background service via `brew services start postgresql@16`).
# In production (Vercel), set this to your hosted Postgres connection string
# (Neon, Supabase, etc.) as a project environment variable instead.
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://user@localhost:5432/landscape_quote_mvp"

# Session cookie signing secret. Any value works locally, but set a real
# random 32+ char secret as a Vercel environment variable before ever
# deploying (e.g. `openssl rand -base64 32`).
SESSION_SECRET="replace-me-in-production"

# Set in production (Vercel) to enable photo uploads via Vercel Blob instead
# of writing to local disk. Created automatically when you add a Blob store
# to your Vercel project (Storage tab) and link it to this project.
# BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN=""

# PostHog analytics. Get these from your PostHog project settings — the
# project API key is meant to be public/client-side, not a secret.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_KEY=""
# NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_HOST="https://us.i.posthog.com"

# Stripe billing — without these, the Plan page falls back to recording
# which tier a contractor picked with no real charge (the pre-billing
# behavior). To actually charge people:
#   1. Create a Stripe account (stripe.com) if you don't have one.
#   2. In the Dashboard, create 3 recurring monthly Prices under Product
#      catalog: Basic $49, Core $149, White-Glove $399 — names/amounts can
#      differ from TIERS in src/lib/tiers.ts, just keep them in sync.
#   3. Developers > API keys > copy the Secret key into STRIPE_SECRET_KEY
#      below (use a test key first, switch to live once you've tested a
#      real checkout end to end).
#   4. Copy each Price's ID (starts with "price_") into the three
#      STRIPE_PRICE_* vars below.
#   5. Developers > Webhooks > Add endpoint, pointing at
#      <your deployed domain>/api/stripe/webhook (this won't work with a
#      localhost URL — use the Stripe CLI's `stripe listen --forward-to
#      localhost:3000/api/stripe/webhook` for local testing instead).
#      Select events: checkout.session.completed,
#      customer.subscription.updated, customer.subscription.deleted.
#      Copy the endpoint's signing secret into STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET.
#   6. Set all of these as real environment variables in Vercel too —
#      values in this file are local-only.
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=""
# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=""
# STRIPE_PRICE_BASIC=""
# STRIPE_PRICE_CORE=""
# STRIPE_PRICE_PREMIUM=""
